      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(-2x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(-2x)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|-2x|\\sqrt{1+(-2x)^{2}}}\\cdot (-2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2|x|\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
